+\subsubsection{Maxwell--SST reciprocal stress complex and blind equilibrium-rank gate}
+\label{sec:rt_maxwell_reciprocal_stress}
+
+\paragraph{Status and historical input.}
+\textbf{[ORTHODOX GRAPHIC-STATICS INPUT / SST RESEARCH TRACK / NOT A NEW FUNDAMENTAL FORCE LAW].}
+Maxwell's reciprocal-figure construction associates forces meeting at a point
+with a closed force polygon in two dimensions and, in the spatial construction,
+with plane faces whose areas are proportional to the corresponding forces
+\cite{Maxwell1864Reciprocal}.  The construction is useful here as an independent
+geometric audit of a resolved SST contact-stress state, not as evidence that an
+SST vortex knot must literally be a bar framework.  Maxwell also showed that a
+mechanical force problem may remain solvable when a perfect reciprocal figure
+cannot be constructed; in such cases a redundant force diagram may still
+represent the force relations.  Therefore strict reciprocal geometry is a
+stronger condition than mechanical equilibrium and must not be used as a
+stand-alone SST falsifier.
+
+\paragraph{Column convention and first-order balance.}
+Let the resolved active strut/kink constraints be $g_j(X)$ and define the
+column matrix
+\begin{align}
+    A_K
+    :=
+    \left[
+        \nabla_X g_1,\ldots,\nabla_X g_M
+    \right]
+    \in\mathbb R^{3N\times M}.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_AK}
+\end{align}
+The column orientation must be fixed before solving.  With the sign convention
+used in Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_contact_residual}, a first-order equilibrium candidate
+obeys
+\begin{align}
+    \mathbf r_K
+    &:=-\nabla_X E_{\rm SST}+A_K\Lambda,
+    \qquad \Lambda\ge0,
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_global_residual}\\
+    \chi_{\rm KKT}
+    &:={\|\mathbf r_K\|_2\over
+    \max(\|\nabla_XE_{\rm SST}\|_2,\epsilon_E)}.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_chi_kkt}
+\end{align}
+Here $\epsilon_E$ is a preregistered numerical floor, not a fitted physical
+parameter.  When the audited functional is polygonal length, the multipliers
+carry the normalization appropriate to that optimization problem; they are not
+thereby physical forces in newtons.
+
+\paragraph{Local reciprocal closure.}
+Partition Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_global_residual} into the three-vector rows
+associated with resolved vertex $i$,
+\begin{align}
+    \mathbf r_i
+    =
+    -\nabla_{X_i}E_{\rm SST}
+    +\sum_{j=1}^{M}(A_K)_{ij}\Lambda_j .
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_local_residual}
+\end{align}
+A Maxwell-style force polygon/polyhedron audit requires local closure, not only
+one small global norm.  A scale-free diagnostic is therefore
+\begin{align}
+    \chi_{\rm loc}
+    :=
+    \max_i
+    {\|\mathbf r_i\|_2\over
+    \max(\|\nabla_{X_i}E_{\rm SST}\|_2,F_{i,\rm ref})},
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_local_closure}
+\end{align}
+where every $F_{i,\rm ref}$ is fixed before unblinding.  The resolution ladder
+must report both $\chi_{\rm KKT}$ and $\chi_{\rm loc}$.
+
+\paragraph{Rank, homogeneous self-stress, and contact mechanisms.}
+The ordinary numerical rank is supplemented by the two fundamental nullspaces
+\begin{align}
+    n_{\rm self}
+    &:={\dim\ker A_K}=M-\operatorname{rank}A_K,
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_selfstress_nullity}\\
+    n_{\rm left}
+    &:={\dim\ker A_K^{\mathsf T}}
+      =3N-\operatorname{rank}A_K.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_left_nullity}
+\end{align}
+The first quantity counts homogeneous self-stress directions before positivity
+is imposed.  The second is a constraint-network mechanism count.  Only after
+subtracting verified rigid motions, reparametrization directions, and any other
+explicit gauge directions may a reduced mechanism number be quoted.  If
+$A_K$ contains only the contact constraints while the full SST Hessian or
+internal elastic operator is omitted, a nonzero reduced left nullity is
+\textbf{[INFORMATIONAL ONLY]} and is not a proof of dynamical instability.
+
+The physically admissible homogeneous load cone is
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal C_+(A_K)
+    :=
+    \ker A_K\cap\mathbb R_{\ge0}^{M}.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_positive_selfstress_cone}
+\end{align}
+Its nontriviality is tested without an arbitrary amplitude by the normalized
+slice
+\begin{align}
+    A_K\lambda=0,
+    \qquad
+    \lambda\ge0,
+    \qquad
+    \mathbf 1^{\mathsf T}\lambda=1.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_positive_selfstress_lp}
+\end{align}
+Existence, support, and a numerical lower bound on the dimension of this slice
+shall be reported separately from the target positive channel rank of
+Sec.~\ref{sec:rt_colored_contact_rank_nine}.  In particular, the number nine
+must not appear in the objective, tolerance, active-set stopping rule, or
+blinding logic of this audit.
+
+\paragraph{Singular-scale precursor diagnostic.}
+Let
+\begin{align}
+    \zeta_K
+    :=
+    {\sigma_{\min}^{+}(A_K)\over\sigma_{\max}(A_K)},
+    \qquad
+    \kappa_{+,K}:=\zeta_K^{-1},
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_singular_ratio}
+\end{align}
+with the numerical rank tolerance preregistered.  Maxwell noted that a frame
+near a special geometric condition may require very large internal forces or
+become loose after a small deformation \cite{Maxwell1864Reciprocal}.  The SST
+translation is deliberately weaker: a reproducible decrease
+$\zeta_K\rightarrow0$ is a \textbf{conditioning warning}.  It may be promoted
+to a pre-Kairos precursor only if, in a time-resolved campaign, it precedes an
+independently defined event marker and the ordering survives mesh, active-set,
+and perturbation refinement.  A small singular value in a static contact
+matrix is not itself a Kairos event.
+
+\paragraph{SST force--area normalization.}
+For a force contribution $\mathbf F_{i\alpha}$ already known in SI newtons,
+define the research-track stress scale and reciprocal area vector
+\begin{align}
+    \Pi_\star
+    &:={\rhohorn\,\vchar^{2}},
+    \qquad [\Pi_\star]={\rm Pa},
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_sst_stress_scale}\\
+    \mathbf A_{i\alpha}^{\star}
+    &:={\mathbf F_{i\alpha}\over\Pi_\star},
+    \qquad [\mathbf A_{i\alpha}^{\star}]={\rm m^2}.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_sst_area_vector}
+\end{align}
+Using the existing v0.8.35 coherence identity
+$F_{\rm swirl}^{\max}=\pi\rc^2\rhohorn\vchar^2$, this becomes
+\begin{align}
+    \boxed{
+    {\|\mathbf A_{i\alpha}^{\star}\|\over\pi\rc^2}
+    =
+    {\|\mathbf F_{i\alpha}\|\over F_{\rm swirl}^{\max}}
+    }.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_sst_area_force_identity}
+\end{align}
+This is \textbf{[DERIVED NORMALIZATION FROM AN EXISTING CALIBRATED IDENTITY]},
+not a new prediction and not an independent determination of
+$F_{\rm swirl}^{\max}$.  If the numerical multipliers have not been converted
+to SI force by a separately declared physical energy/force normalization,
+Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_sst_area_vector} is marked \texttt{N/A}; no reciprocal
+face area in square metres is reported.
+
+\paragraph{Strict reciprocity and the redundancy guard.}
+When an explicit dual-cell incidence complex is supplied, a strict reciprocal
+candidate must check at least that each internal dual face belongs to exactly
+two cells, that the corresponding primal/dual directions satisfy the declared
+orthogonality convention, and that each local oriented face-area sum closes.
+If these incidence conditions fail while Eqs.~\eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_global_residual}
+and \eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_local_residual} converge, the correct status is
+\begin{align}
+    \boxed{
+    \texttt{MECHANICAL-EQUILIBRIUM-PASS / STRICT-RECIPROCITY-FAIL-OR-UNRESOLVED}
+    }
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_redundancy_guard}
+\end{align}
+rather than mechanical falsification.  This preserves Maxwell's explicit
+redundant-diagram case \cite{Maxwell1864Reciprocal}.
+
+\paragraph{Blind relaxed-knot/contact campaign.}
+The preregistered falsifier shall use the following order.
+\begin{enumerate}
+    \item Hash and salt the case identity and family identity before any physical
+    label is exposed to the scorer.  Preserve resolution, thickness convention,
+    and methodological source role because they are required numerical metadata.
+    \item Freeze the SVD tolerance, KKT thresholds, local-closure threshold,
+    contact-shell tolerance, positive-multiplier tolerance, contact-map metric,
+    perturbation amplitudes, and stopping rules before the first unblinded result.
+    \item Use the original constrained Ridgerunner audit geometry for inferred
+    strut/kink reconstruction.  A uniformly arc-length resampled
+    SSTcore/VortexLab copy may be audited only with an explicit transferred
+    contact sidecar, or under a separately preregistered derived-contact test;
+    it is not silently promoted to the constrained audit geometry.
+    \item When solver-supplied strut/kink multipliers exist, preserve them and
+    evaluate their KKT closure independently of a newly fitted NNLS solution.
+    \item For every blinded family, run a resolution ladder and compare the
+    normalized-arclength contact measure, rank, nullities, positivity structure,
+    $\chi_{\rm KKT}$, $\chi_{\rm loc}$, and $\zeta_K$.
+    \item Unblind only after the per-case outputs, convergence summary, source
+    hashes, and frozen preregistration file are immutable.
+\end{enumerate}
+
+\paragraph{Falsifiers and non-falsifiers.}
+The proposed reciprocal-stress interpretation is rejected or demoted for a
+specified knot/contact model if one or more of the following survives matched
+resolution and multistart refinement:
+\begin{enumerate}
+    \item no nonnegative multiplier solution produces convergent first-order
+    equilibrium under the declared $E_{\rm SST}$;
+    \item solver-supplied load-bearing multipliers require reproducibly negative
+    values after the column convention is fixed;
+    \item global KKT convergence hides a non-convergent local closure residual;
+    \item the active contact measure, numerical rank, or positive self-stress
+    structure fails to converge under a fixed thickness convention;
+    \item a claimed pre-Kairos singular-scale precursor is not temporally ordered
+    before an independently detected Kairos event, or the ordering disappears
+    under refinement;
+    \item a physical reciprocal-area claim is made without an independently
+    declared SI force normalization.
+\end{enumerate}
+Conversely, failure of a strict reciprocal polyhedral embedding alone is
+\emph{not} on this list.  It may falsify the stronger geometric-dual claim, but
+not the underlying mechanical equilibrium if the latter remains independently
+solvable.
